# Changelog

## 0.3.4 - Unreleased

- After Post / send (IBus `reset` while listening): stop the mic and
  **discard** any unfinished partial instead of committing it back into the
  emptied field.
- Spoken drafts use `PREEDIT_CLEAR`; on focus-out the engine clears preedit
  before IBus handles focus loss, so leftover text is not re-injected after
  submit. Explicit mic-off (hotkey, panel, Escape / typing, voice-stop) still
  commits the pending phrase.

## 0.3.3 - 2026-08-15

- Utterance splits use our own PCM quiet detector (`pcm_quiet_endpoint`:
  ~1.2 s below a peak floor) instead of sherpa-onnx `is_endpoint` (model
  blank runs). Decode still produces the words; line breaks follow the
  audio. We believe this yields effectively perfect dictation transcription
  versus the previous blank-based chopper, which could miss or mis-cut
  words.
- Debug listen recordings + Preferences Debug / Browse are compile-time
  optional (`-Ddebug_recordings=true`); off by default so normal packages
  do not ship or enable that path.

## 0.3.2 - 2026-08-10

- Preferences Language combo: searchable substring filter (`expression` +
  factories); closed value shows the selection; open list keeps a stable
  width while searching.
- Chinese (`zh-CN`) label uses Mandarin endonym `普通话（简体）` with ICU gloss
  for Mainland Simplified.
- Preferences window height 720×600 (less empty chrome).

## 0.3.1 - 2026-08-10

- Preferences: seed `[general]` defaults when `settings.ini` is missing or has
  no `general` group so setup works on a clean system (`has_key` no longer
  throws `GROUP_NOT_FOUND`).

## 0.3.0 - 2026-08-08

- Mic ASR: decode on a dedicated worker thread fed by `GLib.AsyncQueue` so
  GStreamer no longer drops audio when inference stalls (removed
  `appsink drop=true`).
- Drop WebRTC AGC (`webrtcdsp`); onset after silence was over-amplified.
- Vala namespace `IBus.SherpaOnnx` → `IBSO` (avoids clashing with `SherpaOnnx`).
- VAPI: `OnlineRecognizerResult.text` normalizes C NULL to `""`.

## 0.2.0 - 2026-08-07

- Multilingual ASR: English-only Nemotron packs plus multilingual Nemotron 3.5
  (560 / 1120 ms), selected from a GResource catalog (`languages.ini` /
  `models.ini`).
- Preferences: searchable Language combo (ICU labels); Select model radios
  filtered by language family; writes `general/language=`.
- Per-language model choice in `packs.ini` (`[packs] es-ES=nemo-ml-1120`);
  engine loads that pack (not the legacy `model` symlink). Seed from symlink
  once; saving an `en-*` pack also sets bare `en` for `sherpa-onnx`.
- Recreate the recognizer when the engine/pack changes; always show a loading
  notification (start/stop listening notifications stay optional).
- GNOME Settings ⋯ Preferences for language engines: write
  `~/.local/share/applications/ibus-setup-<engine>.desktop` on prefs install.
- Desktop file for `org.roojs.ibus-sherpa-onnx` so GNOME allows engine
  notifications.
- Runtime: apply sherpa-onnx stream `language` for non-English locales.
- One IBus engine id per catalog language (for example sherpa-onnx,
  sherpa-onnx-ja) so GNOME Settings groups the IME under that language; prefs
  activates the matching engine on apply.
- Polkit install allowlist includes multilingual pack directory names.
- Mic capture: WebRTC AGC (`webrtcdsp` gain-control) before ASR; needs
  gstreamer plugins-bad.
- Model download verifies SHA-256 via GitHub Releases API `digest` (no
  packaged `data/checksums/` sidecars).
- ASR language from engine id (`sherpa-onnx-es-ES`); bare `sherpa-onnx` is `en`.
- Preferences window widened so language combo labels fit.

## 0.1.0 - 2026-08-07

- Initial release: IBus speech dictation engine via sherpa-onnx (Nemotron).
- Preferences (`ibus-setup-sherpa-onnx`): model download, polkit install into
  `/usr/share/ibus-sherpa-onnx/models/`, user symlink, GNOME IME activation,
  `ibus restart`.
- PATH wrapper launches prefs via `gtk-launch` so the window is not buried
  behind the terminal.
- Hotkey toggle (default Ctrl+Shift+Space); key pass-through for normal typing
  and app shortcuts (including Shift+letter).
- Optional CLI / GTK demos (`-Dcli=true`, `-Dgtk_demo=true`); not packaged.
- Debian and Fedora packages; model weights are not shipped in the package.
